Helen — Alfred Travel Social & Paid-Creative Brief

Freshness: 21 July 2026, 08:00 AEST. Overall status: access degraded; no new verified creative signal.

1. Keyword coverage
The required nine-keyword family was attempted through TikTok search, but pages returned shell/login-gated content rather than hydrated cards. Foreplay’s required Instagram + TikTok Organic + TikTok Ads, Over 3 months filter could not be confirmed because the authenticated app target timed out.

2. Foreplay findings
Foreplay access degraded. Browser navigation timed out; no live app-shell text, filter state, or ad cards could be verified. Prior 20 July rows are not reused as fresh evidence.

3. TikTok organic
Access degraded / no visible examples. No hydrated post cards or creator URLs were available.

4. Instagram organic
Platform gated. Search redirected to login; no visible post card or direct post URL was available.

5. TikTok Ads Manager
Not verified in this run. Do not infer that Alfred has no active ads.

6. Best examples
No fresh Foreplay, TikTok, or Instagram example was verified. Sources attempted: https://app.foreplay.co/discovery ; https://www.tiktok.com/search?q=family%20holiday ; https://www.instagram.com/explore/search/keyword/?q=family%20holiday

7. Alfred implications
Hold the existing hypotheses: family constraint → personalised itinerary; one place for the whole trip; creator POV before product reveal; destination-led Japan with kids. Next test: open on tabs/logistics, reveal Alfred within three seconds, then show flights, hotel, activities, and day-by-day output becoming a usable/bookable itinerary. Restore authenticated-session continuity before changing direction.

8. Opportunity ranking
High: family constraint → personalised itinerary demo (54/60 prior directional score).
High: one trip, no tab overload creator UGC (49/60 prior directional score).
Medium: Japan with kids destination-led demo (46/60 prior directional score).
Medium: Sydney/school-holiday utility short (43/60 prior directional score).

9. Notable shift since yesterday
Access has worsened, not signal: yesterday Foreplay and TikTok had partial usable evidence; today Foreplay timed out, TikTok did not hydrate visible cards, and Instagram redirected to login. No quantified creative shift is supportable.

